al Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nExpert Emergency and Specialty Care for Pets in Connecticut and New York\nYour pet is a part of your family, and we understand that facing an emergency or medical situation can be stressful. You can rely on our compassionate, expert emergency team and board-certified specialists to make the process as easy as possible, with updates at every step to put your mind at ease.\nMedVet Norwalk serves as an extension of your family veterinarian, providing comprehensive emergency and specialty pet care to pets in Connecticut and the New York metropolitan area. Our team has the expertise and resources in our state-of-the-art facility to diagnose and treat your beloved pet, focusing on delivering the best outcome.\nWe also offer urgent care for non-life-threatening conditions such as coughing, diarrhea, ear and skin infections, fever, lameness, minor wounds, vomiting, and more.\nIf your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our hospital 24 hours a day, 365 days a year – no appointment is needed.\nMedVet Norwalk Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nSurgery\nOur Hospital Leaders\nKevin Przybylski, DVM, MBA\nMedical Director\nRobin Paradis\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nDaniel Bryant\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAlessandra Chiaramonte\n, VMD, CCRP. Limited to the Practice of Surgery\nSurgery\nRobert Frischer\n, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nInternal Medicine\nHolly Grodecki\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKaitlin Hopke\n, DVM, DACVD®\nDermatology\nGlen K. King\n, DVM, MS, DACVR (Radiation Oncology)\nRadiation Oncology\nJennifer Mahoney\n, DVM, PGDip VetEd, FHEA, DACVIM (Oncology)\nMedical Oncology\nElizabeth Miller\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMichelle Mordukhaev\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMarjorie Owen\n, DVM, MS, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nLauren Pinchbeck\n, DVM, MS, DACVD®\nDermatology\nKevin Przybylski\n, DVM, MBA\nEmergency Medicine\nHeather Rosenblatt\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nShow All Doctors (\n13\n)\n“\nBrought our boy Hunter here for the second time due to a possible seizure. The staff were very kind and straightforward with their advice and care. The woman at the front desk was especially sweet with reassuring words of care. Hunter is doing much better now.”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a Location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
